{
  "schema": "ssam-discover-kind-corpus/2",
  "note": "Family F4 review (2026-10-23): an adversarial corpus of Traditional, Service and Mobile requests worded without the words Traditional or combo box (the kind comes from the capture's module type, from: capture, or from words such as 'mobile app' or 'phone app'), builds worded like questions about SSAM records, and migrations; most are the independent reviewer's wordings. The labels are written by hand from what each module kind can hold, never from the filter's declarations: expect.top lists the capabilities a correct answer leads with (one of them among the first three direct matches), expect.native the capabilities a 'no proven recipe' native call may open instead, expect.none a request the kind cannot hold (the answer must say so, with no forbidden direct match), expect.build a request that must be answered as a build (never as a question about SSAM records), expect.source a migration whose source must be named. forbid lists the capabilities and text routes that must never appear in the answer (any tier) for that item; osui the OutSystems UI app types allowed (absent: not checked).",
